# BARAKUDA Core Rules

- BARAKUDA is a scientific research software platform and correctness is higher priority than speed of edits.
- Preserve deterministic scientific behavior unless a task explicitly asks for scientific changes.
- Keep changes narrowly scoped and aligned to one clear goal per task.
- Treat launch flow, run protocol, report generation, and device registry boundaries as sensitive system contracts.
- Preserve consistency between Acquisition, Optical Tweezers, and AFM module interfaces.
- Prefer explicit assumptions and written rationale over implicit behavior changes.
- When uncertain about domain meaning (timing, units, calibration, report values), stop and ask.
